.docname {Package CLI}
.docauthor {BakingRL}
.include {docs}
.doclang {en}

`@bakingrl/create-plugin` provides two commands:

- `create-bakingrl-plugin` scaffolds trusted v4 packages.
- `bakingrl-plugin` validates, inspects, packs, signs, and locally installs
  trusted v4 packages.

## Templates

```sh
create-bakingrl-plugin my-plugin
create-bakingrl-plugin my-overlay --template overlay-plugin
create-bakingrl-plugin my-native --template native-sidecar-plugin
```

Available templates:

- `extension-plugin`: extension host entry plus a webview contribution.
- `overlay-plugin`: extension host entry plus an overlay contribution.
- `native-sidecar-plugin`: extension host entry plus a Rust JSON-RPC stdio
  sidecar.

Generated packages declare `schemaVersion: "bakingrl.plugin/4"`, and
`bakingrlApi: "2.0.0"`.

## Validate

```sh
bakingrl-plugin validate .
```

Validation checks:

- manifest schema, id, name, version, exact `bakingrlApi: "2.0.0"`, runtime,
  contributes, host-owned settings, and external surfaces;
- built JavaScript entries for extension host and declared visuals;
- sidecar command paths and `jsonrpc-stdio` declarations;
- package-local paths for declared contribution assets and runtime entries;
- absence of bundled Node runtime binaries such as `node`, `node.exe`, or
  `bin/node*`.

Current validation should reject unsupported V4 fields such as `settings.ui`,
`externalSurfaces.web`, and `externalSurfaces.remote`.

## Doctor

```sh
bakingrl-plugin doctor .
```

`doctor` prints a JSON summary of `bakingrlApi`, sidecars, contribution ids,
and build entries.

## Inspect

```sh
bakingrl-plugin inspect .
```

`inspect` prints the normalized v4 manifest surface used by the host:
`schemaVersion`, `bakingrlApi`, `runtime`, `contributes`, and
`externalSurfaces`.

## Pack

```sh
npm run build
bakingrl-plugin pack .
```

`pack` validates the package, writes `manifest.hashes.json`, and creates a
`.brlp` bundle in `dist-bundles/`.

To sign while packing:

```sh
bakingrl-plugin keygen bakingrl-signing-key.json
bakingrl-plugin pack . --sign bakingrl-signing-key.json
```

Do not commit signing keys, signatures, hashes, bundles, or generated build
outputs unless a release process explicitly requires them.

## Local Install

```sh
bakingrl-plugin install-local .
```

This copies the package into the BakingRL app data package directory. Use it
after `npm run build` when testing a package in the host app.

## Marketplace Metadata

The helper can validate marketplace listings and generate release metadata:

```sh
bakingrl-plugin validate-listing .
bakingrl-plugin release-metadata . --bundle-url <url> --listing-url <url> --platform any
bakingrl-plugin marketplace-entry . --developer <id> --bundle-url <url> --listing-url <url> --platform any
```

`--platform` defaults to `any`. Native sidecar packages should publish one
artifact per supported platform using `darwin-arm64`, `darwin-x64`,
`linux-x64`, or `windows-x64`.

Marketplace metadata includes `bakingrlApi`, reviewed `artifacts` with bundle
hashes and signature public keys, review metadata, and other host-facing
package fields.
